description:
Develop a signed magnitude multiplier that takes two 16-bit signed inputs, A and B, and produces a 32-bit signed output, result. The module determines the sign of the result based on the signs of A and B, performing the multiplication on the absolute values of the inputs. If both inputs are negative, the output is positive; if one input is negative, the output is negative. The module effectively handles the signed nature of the inputs and output to ensure correct multiplication results in signed magnitude representation.
module top_module(
    input signed [15:0] A,
    input signed [15:0] B,
    output signed [31:0] result
);

code:
module top_module(
    input signed [15:0] A,
    input signed [15:0] B,
    output signed [31:0] result
);reg signed [31:0] temp_result;
reg sign;

always @(*) begin
    if (A[15] == 1 && B[15] == 1) begin
        temp_result = ~(A[15:0] * B[15:0]) + 1;
        sign = 0;
    end
    else if (A[15] == 1) begin
        temp_result = -A[15:0] * B[15:0];
        sign = 1;
    end
    else if (B[15] == 1) begin
        temp_result = -B[15:0] * A[15:0];
        sign = 1;
    end
    else begin
        temp_result = A[15:0] * B[15:0];
        sign = 0;
    end
end

assign result = (sign == 1) ? -temp_result : temp_result;

endmodule

