Design a speech codec adhering to the G.711 standard that processes a digital input signal. The module takes a 16-bit input signal and outputs a 16-bit quantized value. It incorporates three primary functions: first, it applies a high-pass filter to eliminate unwanted low-frequency noise; second, it performs mu-law encoding to effectively compress the signal's dynamic range; and finally, it quantizes the encoded signal to match the specified bit rate of 64 kbps. This codec is specifically designed for handling speech signals efficiently by preprocessing and encoding them for optimal transmission.
